<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Android Auto Backup, API 26-30 (android:fullBackupContent).

  Records are backed up. Photographs never are. That split is the owner's
  decision, recorded in SPEC-ANDROID 3.1, and the quota is why: Auto Backup
  gives roughly 25 MB, records are irreplaceable, and photographs are
  re-takeable and would blow past it. The ZIP export (AM10) is the photo safety
  net.

  THE RULE THAT SHAPED THE STORAGE LAYOUT. The `path` attribute matches a
  literal path prefix — the format supports no wildcards at all. With photos
  living at watches/<slug>/images/ as originally specified, excluding them would
  need <exclude path="watches/*/images"/>, which cannot be written, or one
  exclude per slug, which cannot be enumerated because slugs are created at
  runtime. The rule as SPEC-ANDROID 3.1 first stated it was not expressible.

  Moving photographs to a top-level media/ tree makes it expressible as two
  static lines. Presence of any <include> makes this include-only, so media/,
  backups/ and cacheDir are excluded by omission rather than by a rule that
  could rot. There is nothing here to keep in sync with the schema.
-->
<full-backup-content>
    <include domain="file" path="watches" />
    <include domain="file" path="config.toml" />
</full-backup-content>
